# channels.conf — channels to bulk-pull with scripts/example-bulk-pull.sh
#
# Format:   CHANNEL_ID   channel-name   # optional comment
# Lines starting with # are ignored. Copy this file to channels.conf (which
# is gitignored: it carries your company's channel ids).
#
# Finding channel IDs:
#   node cli.js list-channels                      # works on most workspaces
#   node cli.js find-channels sre noc ai           # keyword discovery; the fallback
#                                                  # when conversations.list is
#                                                  # admin-restricted (Enterprise Grid)
#   node cli.js channel-toc                        # broad sweep → CHANNELS.md catalog
#
#   Or copy the ID from a Slack permalink:
#     https://yourco.slack.com/archives/CXXXXXXXXXX/p1700000000000000
#                                       ^^^^^^^^^^^ this is the channel ID
#
# Example rows (replace with your own):
# CXXXXXXXXXX   engineering-announcements
# CXXXXXXXXXX   incident-response
# CXXXXXXXXXX   sre
